pico-994A
=========

This project combines code under several licences. All of them must be preserved.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
TI-99/4A emulation core (ti99/, except where noted below)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Ported from DS99/4a (DS994a), Copyright (c) 2023-2026 Dave Bernazzani
(wavemotion-dave) - https://github.com/wavemotion-dave/DS994a

  "For the rest of the code: as long as there is no commercial use (i.e. no
   profit is made), copying and distribution of this emulator, its source code
   and associated readme files, with or without modification, are permitted in
   any medium without royalty provided this copyright notice is used and
   wavemotion-dave is thanked profusely.

   The DS99 emulator is offered as-is, without any warranty."

Thanks profusely, Dave.

DS994a is itself built from several sources, whose terms carry through:

  * TMS9918A video driver - from ColEM by Marat Fayzullin. Retains Marat's
    original copyright statement. Do not reuse that code without trying to
    contact Marat.

  * TMS9900 CPU core - substantially wavemotion-dave's own work, with
    significant scaffolding from Classic99 by Mike Brent (Tursi), used with
    permission. Please adhere to Mike Brent's copyright wishes for any code
    duplicated from Classic99.

  * Disk controller handling - partly from Classic99, likewise with permission.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
ti99/rpk/lowzip.c, lowzip.h  and  ti99/rpk/yxml.c, yxml.h
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
MIT licensed. See ti99/rpk/LICENSE-lowzip.txt and ti99/rpk/LICENSE-yxml.txt.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
ti99/cpu/sn76496/sn76496.c, sn76496.h
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The SN76489/SN76496 PSG core taken unmodified (apart from making three constants
overridable) from pico-smsplus, which carries the SMS Plus lineage by Charles
MacDonald and is distributed under the GNU General Public License.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Port glue, front end and build system (main.cpp, splash.cpp, ti99/ti99_*.c/h,
CMakeLists.txt, scripts)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Copyright (c) 2026 Frank Hoedemakers. Same terms as the rest of the emulator
family (pico-infonesPlus and friends).

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Submodules
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
pico_shared, pico_lib and tusb_xinput carry their own licences; see each repo.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
NOTE ON COMMERCIAL USE
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Because the emulation core is used under a non-commercial licence, this project
as a whole may not be sold or used to make a profit. This is a stricter
condition than the GPL cores used in the sibling emulators in this family.
